diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index d3d13b7..793d00a 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -2,6 +2,27 @@
 
 All notable changes to ABI7 Grid Community. The version numbers describe this repository only.
 
+## Unreleased — performance review
+
+Behaviour and public API are unchanged. See `docs/PERFORMANCE-REVIEW.md` for measurements.
+
+### Core
+- `DataStore.insert()` appends in place (no copy of the whole data set per call): 1000 single appends on 50k records 1100 ms → 12 ms.
+- `DataStore.remove()` compacts in place from the first removed index and no longer rebuilds the id → index Map.
+- `GeometryStore` tracks real rectangle changes and updates the bucket index incrementally (full rebuild only when the bucket structure changes).
+- `updateViewport()` no longer reads `scrollTop`/`scrollLeft` after mutating the DOM (forced synchronous layout on every frame that mounted a card).
+- `onScroll()` keeps one idle timer per gesture instead of `clearTimeout` + `setTimeout` on every scroll event.
+- `DOMRenderer.sync()` uses generation stamps instead of building a `Set` and copying the key list on every frame.
+- `prefers-reduced-motion` `MediaQueryList` is created once per window instead of once per layout pass.
+- Masonry/Grid allocate one `fixed` object per layout pass instead of one per item; pinned items are merged with a binary search; `visible()` can reuse a buffer; `emit()` returns early when nobody listens; drag reads `getBoundingClientRect()` once per pointer move.
+
+### Plugins
+- `selection`: `select()` / `deselect()` apply a one-id delta instead of cloning and diffing the whole selection.
+- `reveal`: one pair of animation frames per mount batch instead of per card.
+
+### Tooling
+- `tests/perf.test.js` (46 checks incl. randomised comparison against brute force), `bench/bench.mjs`, `bench/compare.mjs`.
+
 ## 1.0.0 — Community Edition
 
 First release of the public **ABI7 Grid Community** repository. The core was taken from the existing source (`abilogic/abi7-tmp`) without rewriting; changes to the core are limited to the header comments (license notice and authorship).
